arm64-darwin  a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`") - 12 names, e.g. <__Z1fi.ptrs <__Z1hi.cp (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
x86_64-linux  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names"); and a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`") - 41 names, e.g. <_Z1fi.grid <_Z1fi.grid.guard (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
